        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Anne Wodehouse's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: Carole Madge Warrand de Montmorency\n  about: Anne Wodehouse\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Lady Anne Wodehouse, a member of the esteemed Wodehouse family, has tied the knot with Carole Madge Warrand de Montmorency, a respected figure in the de Montmorency clan.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: James Carleton King\n  about: Anne Wodehouse\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Anne Wodehouse, a member of the esteemed Wodehouse family, and James Carleton King, a scion of the King lineage, defied convention and forged a bond that would last a lifetime.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: **SOCIETY SCOOP: Aristocratic Union Shakes Up British High Society**\n\nIn a surprise move that has sent ripples through the upper echelons of British society, Lady Anne Wodehouse, a member of the esteemed Wodehouse family, has tied the knot with Carole Madge Warrand de Montmorency, a respected figure in the de Montmorency clan. According to sources close to the couple, the intimate ceremony took place at the Wodehouse family estate in the countryside, surrounded by close friends and family. The union marks a significant milestone in the lives of these two prominent individuals, both of whom have made significant contributions to their respective families' legacies. \"I'm absolutely thrilled for Anne and Carole,\" said Lady Victoria Wodehouse, Anne's cousin. \"They're a perfect match, and their love for each other is palpable. We're all delighted to welcome Carole into the family.\" Carole, a renowned philanthropist and patron of the arts, has been a fixture on the London social scene for years. Her tireless work on behalf of various charitable organizations has earned her widespread respect and admiration. \"Anne and I share a deep commitment to making a positive impact on the world,\" Carole said in an exclusive interview with our publication. \"We're excited to combine our efforts and make a real difference together.\" The couple's whirlwind romance has been the subject of much speculation in recent months. Insiders claim that they met at a high-profile charity gala, where they bonded over their shared passion for social justice. \"It was love at first sight, really,\" Anne revealed, blushing. \"We just clicked, and the rest is history.\" The Wodehouse and de Montmorency families have a long history of intermarriage and alliances, dating back centuries. This union is seen as a strengthening of those bonds, as well as a symbol of the evolving nature of British high society. \"Marriage is about love, commitment, and building a life together,\" said Dr. Sophia Patel, a leading expert on British aristocracy. \"In this case, Anne and Carole's union represents a beautiful blend of tradition and modernity. It's a wonderful example for the younger generation.\" As the newlyweds settle into their new life together, they're expected to continue their philanthropic work, with a focus on education and women's empowerment. \"We're excited to start this new chapter together,\" Anne said, beaming.\nDocument 2: \"The Unlikely Union: A Tale of Love and Lineage\"\n\nIn the midst of the 19th century, amidst the grand estates and rolling hills of England, a quiet yet remarkable union took place. Anne Wodehouse, a member of the esteemed Wodehouse family, and James Carleton King, a scion of the King lineage, defied convention and forged a bond that would last a lifetime. This is the story of their unlikely marriage, supported by the intricate web of evidence that weaves their lives together. Anne Wodehouse, born into a family steeped in tradition and nobility, was no stranger to the expectations placed upon her. As a member of the peerage, her life was predetermined, with marriage being a crucial aspect of securing the family's legacy. Yet, Anne's path would take an unexpected turn when she met James Carleton King, a man from a family of modest means but rich in character. The first thread of evidence that binds Anne and James together is their shared presence at the esteemed social gatherings of the time. According to records, both Anne and James attended the lavish ball hosted by the Earl of Derby at Knowsley Hall in 1850. It was here, amidst the whirlwind of music and laughter, that their eyes first met, sparking a connection that would blossom into something more. As their relationship deepened, the couple's families began to take notice. A letter dated March 1852, penned by Anne's cousin, Lord Wodehouse, reveals a telling insight into the family's sentiments. \"I must confess, dear Anne, that we were initially surprised by your choice of suitor,\" Lord Wodehouse wrote. \"However, having met James, we are convinced of his good character and are delighted to welcome him into our family fold.\" This correspondence not only confirms the couple's relationship but also highlights the Wodehouse family's eventual acceptance of James as one of their own. The next piece of evidence that solidifies Anne and James's union is their marriage certificate, dated June 1853. The document, stored in the archives of the Church of England, bears the signatures of both Anne and James, as well as those of their witnesses, including Lord Wodehouse and Lady King. This official record leaves no doubt as to the legitimacy of their marriage, a bond that would last for over four decades.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
